# Artifact Engine

A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for managing artifacts - structured content objects that can be created, versioned, searched, and organized through channels.

## Overview

Artifact Engine provides a complete artifact management system with:
- **Artifact Storage**: Create, read, update, and delete artifacts with full versioning
- **Channel Organization**: Organize artifacts into channels for logical grouping
- **Search Capabilities**: Full-text search with metadata filtering
- **Version History**: Track all changes with the ability to retrieve any version
- **Capability Negotiation**: Dynamic feature discovery and configuration
- **GitHub Integration**: Sync artifacts bidirectionally with GitHub repositories

## Installation

```bash
npm install
npm run build
```

## Usage

### As an MCP Server

```bash
npm start
```

The server runs on stdio by default for MCP communication, or on HTTP port 3002 when running in HTTP mode.

### Environment Variables

- `ARTIFACT_STORAGE_PATH` - Path to store artifacts (default: `./artifacts`)
- `DEFAULT_CHANNEL` - Default channel name (default: `main`)

## MCP Tools

### Artifact Management
- `create_artifact` - Create a new artifact
- `get_artifact` - Retrieve an artifact by ID
- `update_artifact` - Update an existing artifact
- `delete_artifact` - Delete an artifact
- `list_artifacts` - List all artifacts with optional filtering

### Version Control
- `get_artifact_history` - Get version history for an artifact
- `get_artifact_version` - Retrieve a specific version

### Channel Management
- `create_channel` - Create a new channel
- `list_channels` - List all channels
- `get_channel` - Get channel details
- `delete_channel` - Delete a channel

### Search
- `search_artifacts` - Full-text search with filters
- `search_by_metadata` - Search by metadata fields

### GitHub Integration
- `github_push` - Push artifacts to a GitHub repository
- `github_pull` - Pull artifacts from a GitHub repository
- `github_sync` - Bidirectional sync with GitHub
- `github_status` - Check sync status

## Artifact Structure

```typescript
interface Artifact {
  id: string;
  type: string;
  title: string;
  content: string;
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;
  channel: string;
  version: number;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Supported Artifact Types

- `document` - Text documents and notes
- `code` - Source code with language metadata
- `diagram` - Mermaid diagrams and flowcharts
- `data` - JSON/structured data
- `image` - Base64 encoded images
- `template` - Reusable templates
- `config` - Configuration files

## Development

```bash
# Run tests
npm test

# Run with coverage
npm run test:coverage

# Development mode
npm run dev
```

## Architecture

The engine uses a modular architecture:
- `ArtifactStore` - Core storage and versioning logic
- `SearchEngine` - Full-text search implementation
- `CapabilityManager` - Feature negotiation
- `GitHubIntegration` - GitHub sync functionality
- `Handlers` - MCP tool implementations

## License

